From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] unidrv, splwow64: a Linux program's label prints on the driver's paper of its size

Linux Firefox printing a 1 x 2-1/8 inch label across, to the CUPS queue
that prints through DYMO's LabelWriter 550 driver (0922), names its paper
by size alone (PageSize=Custom.595.28x841.89, while the PDF's page is the
label's 153 x 72 points). The page went onto the driver's default paper,
stretched, and on as many labels as the default made pages. splwow64's
print now takes "[P<id>][:<width>x<height>]" -- the PPD paper chosen and the
document's page in points (sgwindrv passes both) -- and prints on the
driver's paper of the page's size, turned when the page is laid out across,
the chosen paper first among papers of that size; a page no paper fits
keeps its proportions on the chosen paper.

The PPD made from the driver had two papers called P262: lw5xx.gpd gives
StandardAddress99010 the OptionID 262 and its seventh paper none, and
Unidrv gave papers without one 256 + their index. Such a paper now gets the
first id from there that no paper of the GPD has, and a PPD leaves out a
paper whose id came before.

Gates: linuxdrv (a page laid out across, paper by size; the test driver
turns for landscape), printdrv (a paper without an OptionID beside one with
its id); mutants PAGEPAPER, PAPERID.
---
--- a/dlls/unidrv/devmode.c
+++ b/dlls/unidrv/devmode.c
@@ -80,7 +80,22 @@
     for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(std_papers); i++)
         if (!_stricmp( name, std_papers[i].name )) return std_papers[i].id;
     if (!strcmp( name, "CUSTOMSIZE" )) return DMPAPER_USER;
-    return 256 + opt;
+    /* a paper of the maker's own: 256 on, past any the GPD gives an option
+     * (DYMO's lw5xx.gpd gives 262 and has a seventh paper without one) */
+    n = 256 + opt;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_PAPERID
+    for (i = 0; i < gpd->features[feature].option_count; i++)
+    {
+        const char *other = gpd_option_attr( gpd, NULL, feature, i, "OptionID" );
+        int m;
+        if (other && gpd_int( gpd, other, &m ) && m == n)
+        {
+            n += gpd->features[feature].option_count;
+            i = -1;
+        }
+    }
+#endif
+    return n;
 }
 
